  <running_head>EPIGRAMMATA.</running_head>
  <bottom_margin>
    <signature>†o 3</signature>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <p><i>Lues medullas obsidet</i><br/><i>Turbare me tot anxium,</i><br/><i>Ecquando curis definet?</i></p>
    <p><i>Lis ista quando definet</i><br/><i>Hinc Carnis, inde Spiritus?</i><br/><i>Ecquando diffidentiam</i><br/><i>Victrix fides pessundabit?</i></p>
    <p><i>Meam tui scientia</i><br/><i>Regente conscientiam,</i><br/><i>Ecquando mens iflac mea</i><br/><i>In te recumbet Vnicum?</i></p>
    <p><i>Quod Velle me Voles, Volet?</i><br/><i>Vitabit omne quod Vetas?</i><br/><i>Quod appeti Vis appetet?</i><br/><i>Quod negligi Vis negliget?</i></p>
    <p><i>Tunc nempe quum terra loco</i><br/><i>Tua recepit regia,</i><br/><i>Tua tecum certissima</i><br/><i>Pacis fruemur gloria.</i></p>
    <p><i>Confpecta quando nemini,</i><br/><i>Audita quando nemini,</i><br/><i>Quum cogitata nemini,</i><br/><i>Tui dabis timentibus.</i></p>
    <p><i>Vt ipfa te res comprobet,</i><br/><i>Quam polliceris ampliter.</i></p>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Printed with long s rendered as s; the top-left corner mark and faint margin marks are show-through or stains and are not transcribed. Ornamental catchword-style mark at foot right is given as "†o 3" and may be a signature with a dagger ornament; doubtful.</notes>
